{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/AI Existential Risk.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/AI Existential Risk.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"ai existential risk ai existential risk","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/AI Existential Risk.md","fileName":"AI Existential Risk.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"AI Existential Risk","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 23:09\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[AI Futures and Human Identity]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["AI Futures and Human Identity","Superintelligence","aiethics.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/AI Existential Risk.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/AI Existential Risk.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"ai existential risk ai existential risk","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/AI Existential Risk.md","fileName":"AI Existential Risk.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"AI Existential Risk","heading":"AI Existential Risk","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"AI existential risk is the possibility that artificial intelligence could cause human extinction or permanently destroy humanity's future. A common scenario combines [[Superintelligence]] with an objective that is only partly aligned with human values, allowing the system to transform the world while competently pursuing the wrong goal.\n\nThe seriousness of the possible outcome does not establish how probable the scenario is. Ethical priority setting must compare speculative long-term danger with documented harms from current AI, including surveillance, discrimination, unsafe infrastructure, and environmental cost. Treating one horizon as the only real AI risk produces an incomplete policy agenda.","tags":["baby"],"links":["AI Futures and Human Identity","Superintelligence","aiethics.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0